EC2 + Jenkins Setup (Ubuntu)

1. Connect to EC2
ssh -i mykey.pem ubuntu@<Public-IP>

2. Update system
sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y

3. Install prerequisites
sudo apt install -y fontconfig openjdk-11-jdk wget gnupg

4. Add Jenkins repo key
wget -O - https://pkg.jenkins.io/debian-stable/jenkins.io.key | sudo tee \
/usr/share/keyrings/jenkins-keyring.asc > /dev/null

5. Add Jenkins repo
echo deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/jenkins-keyring.asc] \
https://pkg.jenkins.io/debian-stable binary/ | sudo tee \
/etc/apt/sources.list.d/jenkins.list > /dev/null

6. Update again
sudo apt update

7. Install Jenkins
sudo apt install -y jenkins

8. Start Jenkins service
sudo systemctl enable jenkins
sudo systemctl start jenkins
sudo systemctl status jenkins

9. Access Jenkins
Browser: http://<Public-IP>:8080
Get initial password:
sudo cat /var/lib/jenkins/secrets/initialAdminPassword
